WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.810
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:15.290
Last time: count the sides, name the shape

3
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:22.660
Chapter 2 · Grids and Coordinates

4
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:28.760
Find any spot, like a treasure map!

5
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:38.670
Aarav and Diya on the tiled terrace

6
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:45.330
Diya: "Your ball is at (4, 2)!"

7
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:56.270
2 across, 4 up… no ball!

8
00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:05.600
He used both numbers. What went wrong?

9
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:16.270
4 across first, then 2 up. Found it!

10
00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:25.200
Grid = lines going across and up

11
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:34.500
Rows go side to side · columns stand tall

12
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:45.180
Start at (0, 0), the origin, bottom left

13
00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:53.500
Coordinates = a point's address, like (4, 2)

14
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.750
1st number: how far across (x)

15
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:04.700
2nd number: how far up (y)

16
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:19.370
(4, 2): 4 across, then 2 up

17
00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:27.750
Walk along, then climb up: across, then up!

18
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:40.130
(4, 2) and (2, 4) are different places!

19
00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:49.690
In (3, 5), which number is across?

20
00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:55.180
3 is across, 5 is up

21
00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:07.680
From (0, 0): 2 across, 3 up. Address?

22
00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:13.280
(2, 3)! Across first, then up

23
00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:28.660
(1, 2) → 3 right → (4, 2)

24
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:40.710
(4, 1) → 2 up → (4, 3)

25
00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:49.100
(5, 3) → 1 left → (4, 3)

26
00:03:49.100 --> 00:04:03.460
(2, 2): 3 right, 2 up, 1 left. Where now?

27
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:14.000
(5, 2) → (5, 4) → (4, 4)!

28
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:26.130
(1, 1) → (1, 5): it moved 4 up

29
00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:35.000
Battleship on a 5 × 5 grid!

30
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:42.800
The ship hides at (3, 4)

31
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:50.750
Diya guesses (4, 3). Hit or miss?

32
00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:57.970
(4, 3) → Miss! The numbers are swapped

33
00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:08.190
(3, 4) → Hit! Across, then up

34
00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:16.720
A screen is a giant grid of pixels

35
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:26.410
Each pixel has an address, like (120, 45)

36
00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:33.570
Colour the right pixels → a picture!

37
00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:37.270
Your turn: practice check

38
00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:47.390
Mark (4, 2). Which number is across?

39
00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:58.990
4 is across: 4 across, then 2 up

40
00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:02.960
A grid has rows and columns

41
00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:07.130
Address = (across, up)

42
00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.130
Across first, then up. Order matters!

43
00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.930
Screens are grids of pixels

44
00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:19.540
Chapter 2 done!

45
00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:26.340
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
